-- title:
--   Invariants of W[[u,v]]/(uv-π) lift to symmetric series
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and write $W[[u,v]]$ for the two-variable power series ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` with variables $u = X_0$, $v = X_1$. Assume that $uv - \pi$, that is $X_0 X_1 - C\,\pi$, is a non-zero-divisor of $W[[u,v]]$. Let $x$ be an element of the crossing model $R_\pi = W[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi)$, the quotient by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C\,\pi$, and assume that $x$ lies in `fixedSubring π`, the equaliser subring of the identity and of `crossingSwap π`; the latter is the ring automorphism of $R_\pi$ induced on the quotient by the automorphism `uvSwapEquiv` of $W[[u,v]]$ that renames the variables along the transposition of the indices $0$ and $1$, i.e. by $u \leftrightarrow v$. In other words, $x$ is invariant under the branch-exchange involution. The conclusion is that $x$ admits a symmetric lift: there exists $F \in W[[u,v]]$ with `uvSwapEquiv F = F`, that is $F(v,u) = F(u,v)$, whose class modulo $uv - \pi$ equals $x$. No hypothesis of $2$-torsion-freeness on $W$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the surjectivity of the map from symmetric power series onto the fixed ring of the involution exchanging the two branches of the crossing $uv = \pi$, the local model at a supersingular or crossing point for the Atkin–Lehner type involution. It feeds the structural descriptions of the fixed ring as a quotient of a power series ring by an Eisenstein equation, [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot) and its variant [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete).
